From d8c4d01b51390541f1a09b71078710bf77fe9832 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(indoor): add an opt-in native-cell door owner
 matcher

directoryDoorReviews/doorCandidates/reviewedDoorPortal accept an optional
DoorOwnerMatcher. The default ("legacy") is the unchanged outline-proximity
matcher and produces identical output.

"native-cell" steps just past each face of the door footprint along its
normal (footprint depth + 0.25/0.5/1/1.5 ft), finds the native wall-bounded
cell there and takes the nearest room by outline among that cell's rooms
(the rule in native_doors.py / door_proposals.py). It decides only for two
different cells with two different, walkable, untied owners; same-cell,
one-sided (exterior) and cell-less doors keep the legacy result. Reviewed
links always win. By default it only fills doors the legacy matcher left
without a portal: a disagreement with a legacy portal is reported as a
conflict, because a merged native cell can omit the real room (audit:
doors 1513453 and 1630256). overrideLegacy and maxOwnerGapFeet are opt-in.

scripts/audit-native-cell-door-owners.ts compares saved door owners with
the rule on derived exports (no master ZIP is read).

